rec='''# Final Recommendations - Suggestions Only\n\n## Winner and integrated concept\n\n**Champion:** #1 Wingman foundation. **Runner-up:** Layered 2D cosmetic rig. **Final Four:** Wingman foundation, Layered 2D cosmetic rig, Weekly mission cosmetic, Collection cabinet. **Elite Eight:** add Provenance nameplate, Reduced-motion static celebration, Item entitlement ledger, No marketplace rule.\n\n### BuffaGo Wingman\n\n**Promise:** Your wing story becomes visible. Give every user the existing Wingman after onboarding. A verified rating, crawl, mission, state or milestone earns a small curated item; the user can equip it on profile and contextual moments. The primary loop is explore -> verify -> earn -> equip -> share. The secondary loop is weekly mission, travel and collection progress. No friends are required.\n\n- **New user:** default mascot plus a first-rating item. **Casual:** may ignore equipment without losing function. **Power user:** permanent travel/crawl prestige.\n- **Configuration:** one frame/nameplate plus up to three mascot slots at launch. Show on profile hero, mission completion, leaderboard row, crawl recap and share card; not continuous navigation/map/rating decoration.\n- **Taxonomy:** launch shirt, hat, accessory, background, frame, nameplate/title; defer body variants, shoes, handhelds, extra archetypes, animation.\n- **Earn / rarity:** verified missions, ratings, crawls, geography and transparent events. Use provenance-first (“earned by...”) with Local/Seasonal/Founder/Challenge Champion as filters, not a scarcity ladder. Achievement ownership is permanent; seasonal visibility archives. No duplicate currency.\n- **Accessibility/safety:** text provenance, non-color signals, high contrast, static reduced-motion reveal, curated layers, no uploads/free text/trade/paid advantage, opt-out public loadout, no exact location cosmetics.\n- **Analytics/flags:** catalog viewed, earn, reveal, equip, profile impression, share, qualified action, motion setting; gate each phase and retain a holdout.\n\n## Top recommendations\n\n### Now\n\n1. Interview/prototype-test adult mascot acceptance and profile visibility.\n2. Define provenance-first catalog, entitlement and moderation policy.\n3. Prove a fixed static layer contract around `wing-user.png`.\n4. Concept-test first-rating and weekly-mission rewards behind a flag.\n5. Add measurement plan and a holdout before interpreting retention.\n\n### Next\n\n6. Collection cabinet and provenance detail.\n7. Profile/leaderboard projection.\n8. Server-authoritative entitlement ledger and asset manifest.\n9. Crawl/travel rewards and shareable recap.\n10. Accessibility snapshots and kill switch.\n\n### Later\n\nGeographic sets, disclosed restaurant collaborations, squads, and static winner celebrations.\n\n### Do not pursue\n\nMarketplace, paid cosmetics, random drops, UGC, social-gated rewards, public precise-location cosmetics, broad body proliferation, app-wide mascot saturation.\n\n## Best picks\n\nBest XS: Provenance nameplate. Best S: First-rating welcome token. Best retention: Weekly mission cosmetic. Best sharing: Mascot share card. Best cold start: No-friends starter collection. Best mission reward: Mission choice reward. Best profile: Profile hero card. Best collectible: Wing passport shelf. Best accessibility: Reduced-motion static celebration. Best technical foundation: Item entitlement ledger. Most overrated: app-icon personalization. Most underrated: provenance nameplate. Best combination of three: Wingman foundation + layered rig + provenance nameplate.\n\n## Phased roadmap\n\n| Phase | Objective | Include | Exclude | Exit / kill |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 0 Validate | prove adult fit | interviews, static mockups, preference tests | build | >=60% comprehension; kill if childish/trust concern |\n| 1 Minimum lovable | visible earned identity | default mascot, 1-3 slots, profile, first-rating/weekly reward | commerce, animation, UGC | equip + mission lift; kill if <15% eligible equip |\n| 2 Progression | durable stories | provenance, collection, leaderboard, share card | teams/partners | incremental qualified action/D7 with holdout |\n| 3 Social | optional identity | crawl recap, winner screen, comparison | gifting/trading | opt-in without pressure/safety complaints |\n| 4 Expand | test locality | geography, transparent events | archetype proliferation | repeat exploration/partner trust |\n\n**Risks / kill criteria:** stop or roll back if rating/crawl completion declines, accessibility fails, trust/safety complaints rise, opt-in/equip adoption is weak, or holdout cannot show incremental value. All recommendations are suggestions only; no implementation occurred.\n'''
(o/'final-recommendations.md').write_text(rec,encoding='utf8')
